The forebrain binary statically links the following third-party libraries:

- daulet/tokenizers (MIT) — Go bindings for the HuggingFace tokenizers library,
  https://github.com/daulet/tokenizers
- HuggingFace tokenizers (Apache License 2.0) — the Rust tokenization library,
  https://github.com/huggingface/tokenizers
- tiktoken-rs (MIT) — Rust bindings for OpenAI's tiktoken,
  https://github.com/zurawiki/tiktoken-rs
- Oniguruma (BSD 2-Clause) — regular expressions used by tokenizers,
  https://github.com/kkos/oniguruma

The binary also statically links the database drivers a state database hosted
on MySQL or PostgreSQL is reached through (both pure Go):

- go-sql-driver/mysql 1.10.1 (Mozilla Public License 2.0) — MySQL protocol
  driver, https://github.com/go-sql-driver/mysql
- jackc/pgx/v5 5.12.0 (MIT) — PostgreSQL protocol driver, used through its
  database/sql adapter, https://github.com/jackc/pgx

The tokenizer files under assets/tokenizers are third-party works. Each
directory carries its own LICENSE, and assets/tokenizers/README.md records the
source repository and license of every file.

The embedded web frontend (frontend/, built into pkg/gateway/dist) bundles the
following third-party libraries. Both are loaded only when a delivered file of
their kind is previewed:

- docx-preview 0.4.1 (Apache License 2.0) — renders a delivered .docx in the
  browser, https://github.com/VolodymyrBaydalka/docxjs
- SheetJS Community Edition, published as xlsx 0.20.3 (Apache License 2.0) —
  parses a delivered spreadsheet in the browser. Installed from SheetJS's own
  distribution, https://cdn.sheetjs.com/xlsx-0.20.3/xlsx-0.20.3.tgz, because
  the npm package of that name stops at 0.18.5.

